<title>USA: KinderCare issues $300 million 144A notes.</title>
<headline>KinderCare issues $300 million 144A notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue of high-yield debt from KinderCare Learning Centers Inc was priced in the 144A private placement market on Monday, according to a high-yield syndicate source.</p>
<p>The deal was increased in size by $100 million. A separate bank debt portion was decreased from $190 million to $90 million, the source added.</p>
<p>Chase Securities was lead manager on the deal.</p>
<p>BORROWER KINDERCARE LEARNING CENTERS INC</p>
<p>AMT $300 MLN	 COUPON 9.50 PCT   MATURITY 2/15/2009</p>
<p>TYPE SNR SUB NOTES ISS PRICE 100.00  FIRST PAY DATE 8/15/97 LAST MOODY'S B3    YIELD 9.50 PCT    PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P B-MINUS			   CALLABLE NON-CALL FIVE</p>
<p>NOTE: Three-year equity call for 40 pct at par plus coupon U.S. corporate bond unit, 212 859-1672</p>
</text>
